WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.779
Wh- Questions.

2
00:00:02.059 --> 00:00:05.387
Day 4 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.137 --> 00:00:08.161
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:14.628
Today's goal: ask for any information you need (where, when, how much, how long, why) with the right word order.

5
00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:16.831
Part 1.

6
00:00:17.111 --> 00:00:18.263
The question words.

7
00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:20.857
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:23.313
Word, and Asks about, and Example.

9
00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:24.255
What.

10
00:00:24.535 --> 00:00:26.519
Asks about: thing, information.

11
00:00:26.799 --> 00:00:27.673
Example:

12
00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:30.215
What is your name? / What time is it?

13
00:00:30.495 --> 00:00:31.156
Where.

14
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:32.780
Asks about: place.

15
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:33.935
Example:

16
00:00:34.215 --> 00:00:35.559
Where is platform 5?

17
00:00:35.839 --> 00:00:36.457
When.

18
00:00:36.737 --> 00:00:38.103
Asks about: time.

19
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.257
Example:

20
00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:40.988
When does the shop open?

21
00:00:41.268 --> 00:00:41.951
Why.

22
00:00:42.231 --> 00:00:43.809
Asks about: reason.

23
00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:44.964
Example:

24
00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.737
Why is the flight delayed?

25
00:00:47.017 --> 00:00:47.679
Who.

26
00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:49.452
Asks about: person.

27
00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:50.607
Example:

28
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.529
Who is the project manager?

29
00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:53.535
Which.

30
00:00:53.815 --> 00:00:55.649
Asks about: choice from a group.

31
00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:56.804
Example:

32
00:00:57.084 --> 00:00:58.791
Which bus goes to the airport?

33
00:00:59.071 --> 00:00:59.839
Whose.

34
00:01:00.119 --> 00:01:01.505
Asks about: owner.

35
00:01:01.785 --> 00:01:02.660
Example:

36
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.369
Whose laptop is this?

37
00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:05.311
How.

38
00:01:05.591 --> 00:01:07.852
Asks about: way, method, condition.

39
00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:09.007
Example:

40
00:01:09.287 --> 00:01:11.804
How do I get to the metro? / How are you?

41
00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:14.050
How much.

42
00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.762
Asks about: price, uncountable amount.

43
00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:17.917
Example:

44
00:01:18.197 --> 00:01:21.098
How much is this? / How much water do you need?

45
00:01:21.378 --> 00:01:22.274
How many.

46
00:01:22.554 --> 00:01:24.410
Asks about: countable number.

47
00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.565
Example:

48
00:01:25.845 --> 00:01:27.274
How many people are coming?

49
00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:28.450
How long.

50
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.373
Asks about: duration.

51
00:01:30.653 --> 00:01:31.527
Example:

52
00:01:31.807 --> 00:01:33.450
How long does the journey take?

53
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:34.669
How often.

54
00:01:34.949 --> 00:01:36.570
Asks about: frequency.

55
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.725
Example:

56
00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:39.562
How often does the bus come?

57
00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:40.759
How far.

58
00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:42.554
Asks about: distance.

59
00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:43.709
Example:

60
00:01:43.989 --> 00:01:45.567
How far is the hospital?

61
00:01:45.847 --> 00:01:46.701
What time.

62
00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:48.730
Asks about: exact time.

63
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:49.885
Example:

64
00:01:50.165 --> 00:01:51.743
What time does the train leave?

65
00:01:53.093 --> 00:01:53.968
Part 2.

66
00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:55.208
The formula.

67
00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:57.802
Here is a quick table:

68
00:01:58.082 --> 00:02:01.410
Wh-, and Helper, and Subject, and Verb or rest.

69
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:02.351
Where.

70
00:02:02.631 --> 00:02:03.762
Helper: is.

71
00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:05.813
Subject: the ticket counter.

72
00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:07.181
Verb or rest: ?

73
00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:08.079
When.

74
00:02:08.359 --> 00:02:09.511
Helper: does.

75
00:02:09.791 --> 00:02:11.114
Subject: the train.

76
00:02:11.394 --> 00:02:13.015
Verb or rest: leave?

77
00:02:13.295 --> 00:02:14.191
How much.

78
00:02:14.471 --> 00:02:15.602
Helper: did.

79
00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:17.141
Subject: you.

80
00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:18.935
Verb or rest: pay?

81
00:02:19.215 --> 00:02:19.898
Why.

82
00:02:20.178 --> 00:02:21.287
Helper: are.

83
00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:22.826
Subject: you.

84
00:02:23.106 --> 00:02:24.642
Verb or rest: late?

85
00:02:24.922 --> 00:02:26.010
Which platform.

86
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.442
Helper: does.

87
00:02:27.722 --> 00:02:29.450
Subject: the Chennai train.

88
00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.586
Verb or rest: leave from?

89
00:02:31.866 --> 00:02:32.762
How long.

90
00:02:33.042 --> 00:02:34.194
Helper: will.

91
00:02:34.474 --> 00:02:35.626
Subject: it.

92
00:02:35.906 --> 00:02:37.335
Verb or rest: take?

93
00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:38.277
What.

94
00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:39.751
Helper: can.

95
00:02:40.031 --> 00:02:40.906
Subject:

96
00:02:41.186 --> 00:02:41.869
I.

97
00:02:42.149 --> 00:02:43.599
Verb or rest: do?

98
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:45.845
Part 3.

99
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:48.728
From statement to question: step by step.

100
00:02:49.978 --> 00:02:50.874
Statement:

101
00:02:51.154 --> 00:02:52.498
The bus leaves at 6.

102
00:02:52.778 --> 00:02:57.173
Find what you want to ask about: at 6, then a time, then When or What time.

103
00:02:57.453 --> 00:03:01.677
Add the helper: the verb is leaves (present, he or she or it), then does.

104
00:03:01.957 --> 00:03:04.047
Base verb: leaves, then leave.

105
00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:05.202
Question:

106
00:03:05.482 --> 00:03:07.061
What time does the bus leave?

107
00:03:08.411 --> 00:03:09.755
Here is a quick table:

108
00:03:10.035 --> 00:03:12.189
Statement, and Ask about, and Question.

109
00:03:12.469 --> 00:03:13.643
She lives in Pune.

110
00:03:13.923 --> 00:03:15.224
Ask about: place.

111
00:03:15.504 --> 00:03:16.379
Question:

112
00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:17.747
Where does she live?

113
00:03:18.027 --> 00:03:20.075
The room costs 3,000 rupees.

114
00:03:20.355 --> 00:03:21.699
Ask about: price.

115
00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:22.853
Question:

116
00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.755
How much does the room cost?

117
00:03:25.035 --> 00:03:26.656
I'm late because of traffic.

118
00:03:26.936 --> 00:03:28.387
Ask about: reason.

119
00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:29.541
Question:

120
00:03:29.821 --> 00:03:30.909
Why are you late?

121
00:03:31.189 --> 00:03:32.491
Ravi fixed the bug.

122
00:03:32.771 --> 00:03:34.691
Ask about: person (subject).

123
00:03:34.971 --> 00:03:35.845
Question:

124
00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:37.235
Who fixed the bug?

125
00:03:37.515 --> 00:03:38.773
They met last week.

126
00:03:39.053 --> 00:03:40.355
Ask about: time.

127
00:03:40.635 --> 00:03:41.509
Question:

128
00:03:41.789 --> 00:03:42.920
When did they meet?

129
00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.038
Info:

130
00:03:45.318 --> 00:03:47.942
Special case: who or what as the subject.

131
00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:51.721
When who or what is the subject, don't add do or does or did:

132
00:03:52.001 --> 00:03:53.003
Who called you?

133
00:03:53.283 --> 00:03:54.947
(someone called), What happened?

134
00:03:55.227 --> 00:03:56.315
Who did call you?

135
00:03:57.665 --> 00:03:58.583
Part 4.

136
00:03:58.863 --> 00:04:00.911
Indirect questions: more polite.

137
00:04:02.161 --> 00:04:06.555
Start with a polite phrase, then use statement order (no do or does or did):

138
00:04:07.905 --> 00:04:09.249
Here is a quick table:

139
00:04:09.529 --> 00:04:11.385
Direct, and Polite (indirect).

140
00:04:11.665 --> 00:04:12.903
Where is the station?:

141
00:04:13.183 --> 00:04:14.868
Could you tell me where the station is?

142
00:04:15.148 --> 00:04:16.599
What time does it open?:

143
00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:18.564
Do you know what time it opens?

144
00:04:18.844 --> 00:04:20.231
How much does it cost?:

145
00:04:20.511 --> 00:04:22.175
Can I ask how much it costs?

146
00:04:22.455 --> 00:04:23.671
When will it be ready?:

147
00:04:23.951 --> 00:04:25.871
Could you let me know when it will be ready?

148
00:04:27.221 --> 00:04:31.274
Use indirect questions with strangers, officials and senior people.

149
00:04:32.624 --> 00:04:33.584
Part 5.

150
00:04:33.864 --> 00:04:36.787
Conversation: at a railway enquiry counter.

151
00:04:38.037 --> 00:04:40.063
Here is how the conversation goes.

152
00:04:40.343 --> 00:04:41.581
Excuse me.

153
00:04:41.861 --> 00:04:44.442
Which train goes to Mysuru this evening?

154
00:04:44.722 --> 00:04:47.389
There's the Chamundi Express at 6:15.

155
00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:49.653
Which platform does it leave from?

156
00:04:49.933 --> 00:04:51.149
Platform 8.

157
00:04:51.429 --> 00:04:53.285
How long does the journey take?

158
00:04:54.635 --> 00:04:56.235
The conversation continues.

159
00:04:56.515 --> 00:04:57.837
About three hours.

160
00:04:58.117 --> 00:05:00.485
How much is a second-class ticket?

161
00:05:00.765 --> 00:05:02.472
110 rupees.

162
00:05:02.752 --> 00:05:06.080
And how often do trains go to Mysuru on Sundays?

163
00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.981
Every two hours, roughly.

164
00:05:09.331 --> 00:05:10.931
The conversation continues.

165
00:05:11.211 --> 00:05:14.966
Could you tell me where the ticket counter for reserved tickets is?

166
00:05:15.246 --> 00:05:17.422
It's on the first floor, near the escalator.

167
00:05:17.702 --> 00:05:19.089
Thank you very much!

168
00:05:20.439 --> 00:05:21.377
Part 6.

169
00:05:21.657 --> 00:05:22.575
Practice.

170
00:05:23.825 --> 00:05:24.465
1.

171
00:05:24.745 --> 00:05:30.057
Choose the question word: what, where, when, why, who, which, how much, how long. is your office?

172
00:05:30.337 --> 00:05:32.001
(place) 2. is this shirt?

173
00:05:32.281 --> 00:05:34.051
(price) 3. did you call me?

174
00:05:34.331 --> 00:05:36.763
(reason). colour do you want: red or blue?

175
00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:38.707
5. does the movie last?

176
00:05:40.057 --> 00:05:40.975
Success:

177
00:05:41.255 --> 00:05:42.108
Answers.

178
00:05:42.388 --> 00:05:43.220
Where 2.

179
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.524
How much 3.

180
00:05:44.804 --> 00:05:45.721
Why 4.

181
00:05:46.001 --> 00:05:46.919
Which 5.

182
00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:48.095
How long.

183
00:05:49.445 --> 00:05:50.149
2.

184
00:05:50.429 --> 00:05:52.434
Make a question about the bold part.

185
00:05:52.714 --> 00:05:54.143
The meeting starts at 4.

186
00:05:54.423 --> 00:05:55.127
2.

187
00:05:55.407 --> 00:05:56.623
He bought a new phone.

188
00:05:56.903 --> 00:05:57.650
3.

189
00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.359
We stayed for three days.

190
00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:00.343
4.

191
00:06:00.623 --> 00:06:01.925
Meena booked the hotel.

192
00:06:03.275 --> 00:06:04.192
Success:

193
00:06:04.472 --> 00:06:05.325
Answers.

194
00:06:05.605 --> 00:06:07.248
What time does the meeting start?

195
00:06:07.528 --> 00:06:08.232
2.

196
00:06:08.512 --> 00:06:09.536
What did he buy?

197
00:06:09.816 --> 00:06:10.563
3.

198
00:06:10.843 --> 00:06:12.165
How long did you stay?

199
00:06:12.445 --> 00:06:13.149
4.

200
00:06:13.429 --> 00:06:14.624
Who booked the hotel?

201
00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:16.721
3.

202
00:06:17.001 --> 00:06:18.131
Make these polite.

203
00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:21.398
Where is the washroom? / When will my order arrive?

204
00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:23.665
Success:

205
00:06:23.945 --> 00:06:24.799
Answers.

206
00:06:25.079 --> 00:06:29.708
Could you tell me where the washroom is? / Could you let me know when my order will arrive?

207
00:06:31.058 --> 00:06:31.997
Part 7.

208
00:06:32.277 --> 00:06:33.322
Speak today.

209
00:06:34.572 --> 00:06:38.327
Ask 3 wh- questions at a shop, counter or office.

210
00:06:38.607 --> 00:06:41.551
Ask one indirect question to someone you don't know.

211
00:06:41.831 --> 00:06:44.988
At work, replace Any update? with a specific question:

212
00:06:45.268 --> 00:06:47.188
When do you think the PR will be ready?

213
00:06:48.538 --> 00:06:50.074
That's the end of this lesson.

214
00:06:50.354 --> 00:06:55.005
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

215
00:06:55.285 --> 00:07:01.407
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

